@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix mig: <https://semblance.dev/ns/migration#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:app-bar-one-row a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "An app bar is one row while it fits: its actions and end actions in one group after the brand"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/570> ;
    chg:motivation """A bar with c:endActions was two rows on every screen wider than medium, however wide: a grid
gave the brand a row of its own, so a desktop bar had a first row of the logo and the name with the rest of its
width empty. The grid was there to keep the end actions in line with the actions, which a plain wrapping row
cannot promise for three groups; one group of the actions and the end actions can.""" ;
    chg:substance """c:AppBar renders its actions and its end actions in one group after the brand: a div with
class sem-tools holding the actions' div (sem-actions) and, when there are c:endActions, the end actions' div
(sem-end). The header's children are the brand and that group; before, they were the brand, the actions and the
end actions. The text rendering is unchanged.

Styles: on a screen wider than medium the bar wraps by its content, with no breakpoint for it: one row while the
brand and the group fit (the brand, then the actions, then the end actions at the row's inline end); the group on
a row of its own below the brand when they do not, the end actions at that row's inline end, in line with the
actions' first line, the actions wrapping within their own room. The grid is gone. A bar without end actions
lays out as before #565 (the actions after the brand, at the row's end while they share it). On a compact or
medium screen the bar is the one row as before, the end actions after the More button; a theme that lays the
actions' children out in the header itself (Semblance's page strip) sets the group to display: contents too.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Nothing in the graph moves. A style of your own that selects the bar's parts as the
header's children moves one level down: [data-sem-c=app-bar] > .sem-actions becomes
[data-sem-c=app-bar] > .sem-tools > .sem-actions, and > .sem-end becomes > .sem-tools > .sem-end. A theme that
gives the actions display: contents to place their children among the header's gives the sem-tools group
display: contents as well.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Nothing in the graph moves. Selectors of your own written against sem-tools go back to the
header's children (drop the > .sem-tools step); the bar is again two rows wherever it has end actions on a
screen wider than medium.""" ;
    chg:affects c:AppBar .
